# Booking → Services → Timetable → Schedule & Covers → Overview

## Chain (product law)

```
Booking (plazas) → Services (clients / seats) → Timetable (staff) → Schedule & Covers (day patches) → Overview (paint)
```

| Layer | Owns | Does not own |
|-------|------|----------------|
| **Booking Portal** | Public AS/weekend Places (capacity / taken / free) | Instructor names; DC; Bespoke |
| **Services** (Admin `c4k_services`) | Who is booked on each seat (term / trial); **DC phased/dated seats** from `portal_capacity_chain_occupants.js` | Day-of covers |
| **Timetable** (Admin Instructor timetable) | Who works which seat / hours — base `autumn_staff_hours_reference.js` + **`portal_staff_timetable_cells`** | Public Places |
| **Schedule & Covers** | Day exceptions (`schedule_overrides` + `staff_unavailability`) | Term-wide capacity redesign |
| **Sessions Overview** | **Only day look-here** — capacity chain standing (Places AS + Services DC phases + Timetable Bespoke) + live Covers | Authoring drafts; WEEK1/Fadi/Mon14 canonical boards for Overview paint |

## Capacity chain (Overview standing)

- Shared resolver: `working_ui/portal/portal_overview_capacity_chain.js`
- Deployed seats: `working_ui/portal/portal_capacity_chain_occupants.js` (`PORTAL_CAPACITY_CHAIN_OCCUPANTS`)
- DC phases helper: `working_ui/portal/portal_dc_services_local.js`
- Admin Services paints DC via `PortalDcServicesLocal.boardForIso` (phase badges)
- Admin Timetable saves to Supabase; Admin refresh merges cells into hours before chain resolve
- Capacity chain does **not** read `term_timetable_local_hours_draft_v1` (retired twin)
- Admin Overview calls `portalResolveStaffDashboardSource({ forSessionsOverview: true })` and skips `resolveAutumnInstructorsForCalendarDate` when `capacityChainNoCanonicalRemap`
- Staff Today uses the same capacity chain (staff-scoped rows). Day patches still from `schedule_overrides`

## Capacity rule (AS / weekend)

- Public `capacity` = standing **seat line count** for that band (`booked` + `NO PARTICIPANT` / open lines).
- **Do not** inflate capacity from `instructorCount` (phantom Places).
- Intentional hardcap only: **Sunday SwimFarm Multi-Activity = 6** (product band). Document any new hardcap here before coding.
- Wed Multi Acton is filtered off the public offer (not a Places band).

## Trials on Places

- Active trial (pay hold / paid one-session before term convert) **occupies a Place** (taken++, openSeats--).
- **Office look** (Open Places seats): label `HOLD BY TRIAL - {Name}` on that seat — not CLIENT standing.
- **Public Booking**: no participant names; parents only see free/taken capacity.
- When they pay for term → CLIENT standing name. When they release / EOD no decision → seat back to `NO PARTICIPANT`.
- Do **not** fold trials into MADRE as normal CLIENT seats; reservation hold + dated Overview override remain the ops path until convert.

## Day Centre / Bespoke

- Never appear as Booking Places.
- **Do** appear on Admin Services: DC as **phased/dated seat lines** (who-with-whom + windows) from occupants.
- Deployed `portal_capacity_chain_occupants.js`: `day_centre` slots with `phase`, `validFrom`/`validTo`, `seatLines`.
- Overview / Covers read DC from those seats; Timetable owns staff hours; Covers own day exceptions.
- Standing from **20 Sep** is term truth; earlier phases are explicit Services seats until then.
- Admin create/edit seat only for new programme seats or term replan — not day-of.

## Look-here

- Day: **Sessions Overview** only (Admin).
- Do not author new DC / Sunday phases on localhost LOCAL boards — use Admin Services + Instructor timetable.
- Admin Open Places uses the same live offer payload as Booking (`SLOTS`).

## Admin editors (production)

1. Places / Open Places · 2. Services (`#c4k_services`) · 3. Instructor timetable (`#roster_spreadsheets`) · 4. Schedule & Covers · 5. Sessions Overview
Legacy LOCAL HTML paths redirect into Admin.

## When changing offer capacity

Edit `supabase/functions/_shared/portal_booking_seat_helper.ts` → deploy `portal-booking-offer`. Smoke that sample AS/weekend bands match seat lines and DC/Bespoke are absent.
